==English==
[[File:2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg|right|thumb|Chocolate-chip '''cookies'''.]]
[[File:Peanut_butter_cookies,_September_2009.jpg|right|thumb|Soft '''cookies''' which do not contain chips, fruit or nuts.]]
[[File:Oreo-Two-Cookies.jpg|right|thumb|Layered chocolate '''cookies'''.]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkʊki/}}, {{enPR|ko͝ok'i}}
** {{audio|en|En-au-cookie.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkuːki/|a=sometimes in <<Northern England>>}}, {{enPR|ko͞ok'i}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkʉke/|/-kɪ/|/-ki/|a=Scotland,NI}}
* {{homophones|en|kooky<aa:<<foot-goose>>,some other <<UK>> pronunciations>}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʊki|uːki|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=biscuit|:bor|nl:koekje<alt:koekie>|tree=1}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|nl|koekie}}, dialectal diminutive of {{m|nl|koek|t=cake}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*kōkô}} (compare {{cog|nds-de|Kookje|t=biscuit, cookie, cracker}}, {{cog|nds|Kook|t=cake}}, {{cog|de|Kuchen|t=cake}}). More at {{m|en|cake}}. Not related to {{ncog|en|cook}}.

The computing senses derive from {{m|en|magic cookie}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|en|cookey|cooky||dated}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|North America|Philippines}} A small, flat, baked good which is either crisp or soft but firm.
#: {{syn|en|biscuit|bickie|l2=UK,Australia}}
# {{lb|en|UK|Commonwealth}} A sweet baked good (as in the previous sense) usually having chocolate chips, fruit, nuts{{,}} etc. baked into it.
# {{lb|en|Scotland}} A [[bun]].
# {{senseid|en|Q178995}}{{lb|en|computing|internet|ellipsis}} An [[HTTP cookie]].
# {{senseid|en|magic cookie, in computing}} {{lb|en|computing|ellipsis}} A {{l|en|magic cookie}}.
# {{lb|en|slang|dated}} An attractive young woman.
# {{lb|en|slang|vulgar|euphemistic}} The [[vulva]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=T. R. Oulds|title=Story of Many Secret Night|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=YVjrAQAAQBAJ&pg=PT41&dq=&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q&f=false|publisher=Lulu.com|year_published=2010|isbn=9781409285816
|passage=Her legs hung over the edge and the large towel covered just enough of her lap to hide her ''''cookie''''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Lennie Ross|title=Blow me|pageurl=http://books.google.ca/books?id=aqi9-p-eggEC&pg=PA47&dq=%22her+cookie%22|page=47|publisher=Lulu.com|year_published=2010|isbn=9781257133819
|passage=If she wanted to compete in this dog-eat-pussy world, she had to keep up her personal grooming, even if it meant spreading her legs and letting some Vietnamese woman rip the hair off her '''cookie''' every other week.}}
#* '''2014''', {{w|Nicki Minaj}}, "{{w|Anaconda (Nicki Minaj song)|Anaconda}}" (Clean Version), ''{{w|The Pinkprint|The Pinkprint}}'':
# {{lb|en|slang|vulgar|LGBT}} The [[anus]] of a [[man]].
# {{lb|en|slang|drugs}} A piece of [[crack cocaine]], larger than a [[rock]], and often in the shape of a cookie.
#: {{hyper|en|pie}}
# {{lb|en|informal|in plural}} One's eaten food (e.g. lunch, etc.), especially one's stomach contents.
#: {{ux|en|I lost my '''cookies''' after that roller coaster ride.}}
#: {{ux|en|I feel sick, like I'm about to [[toss one's cookies|toss my '''cookies''']].}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} {{clipping of|en|fortune cookie}}.
# {{lb|en|Northern US}} A [[doughnut]]; a peel-out or [[skid mark]] in the shape of a circle.

